    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the product of the fractions \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\), we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together. Then we simplify the resulting fraction if necessary.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. Identify the numerators and denominators of the fractions.\n   - The first fraction is \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\).\n   - The second fraction is \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\).\n\n2. Multiply the numerators.\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 3 = 3\n   \\]\n3. Multiply the denominators.\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 7 = 35\n   \\]\n4. Form the resulting fraction.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1 \\times 3}{5 \\times 7} = \\frac{3}{35}\n   \\]\n\nThe fraction \\(\\frac{3}{35}\\) is already in its simplest form because 3 and 35 have no common divisors other than 1. Therefore, the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{35}}\\).",
